    "In-App Event texts follow Apple’s In-App Events guidance (Guideline 2.3.13): no specific prices or discounts (App Review rejects them; set a needed purchase as the purchase requirement), no unverifiable claims like “the best” or “#1”, no all capitals or repeated punctuation, no other platforms (2.3.10), no placeholder text (2.1), and “For Kids” only in the Kids Category (2.3.8). The name is the event’s real name in title case, not a call to action or the event type. Descriptions use sentence case and describe the event, not the app. Texts that break a rule are refused with the reason." : {
